      "rule": "Self-review and self-approval are blocked by default; the same member cannot review or approve a record they authored or own."
    },
    {
      "id": "D03-06",
      "doc": "m0-d03-roles-and-separation-of-duties.md",
      "rule": "An Org Admin may record a separation-of-duties waiver that is time-bound, reason-required, and scoped to a record type, recording scope, beneficiary, approver, rationale, and expiry."
    },
    {
      "id": "D03-07",
      "doc": "m0-d03-roles-and-separation-of-duties.md",
      "rule": "A separation-of-duties waiver must be approved by a second person who is an Org Admin and is not the member the waiver benefits; a sole Org Admin cannot waive their own conflict."
    }
  ],
  "decides": "A waiver is requested by an Org Admin with a required reason, a scope of record type, recording scope and beneficiary, and an expiry after the request; it is approved by a second Org Admin who is not the beneficiary, so a sole Org Admin cannot waive their own conflict. Without a waiver self-review and self-approval stay refused. The Compliance Lead alone approves acknowledgement waivers of at most 12 months, and waived people count as excepted, never acknowledged.",
